# MAGIC %md # 4. Smoking
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Smoking status is defined using a selection group to prioritise records from the different time periods around the baseline date.
# MAGIC <br> Where x is the difference in years from the record date to the baseline date, the priority groups **for smoking** are defined as follows:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **1.** -20 <= x < 0 (**20 years before**)
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **2.** 0 <= x < +0.25 (3 months after)
# MAGIC
# MAGIC That is, only where a smoking record cannot be found before baseline, will records be looked at 3 months after.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Note that smoking status can change over time and *smoking upgrades* will be considered. A person may have historic records indicating that they are a current smoker but more recent records (closest to baseline) indicating that they have never smoked. In this case the historical records should be considered in order to potentially upgrade the person from a non-smoker to an ex-smoker.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md ## 4.1 Codematch all

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md First, we extract all the smoking records for each individual between the pre-defined extreme censor start and end dates via simple inner join with the codelist.

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Match all smoking records
gdppr_smoking = gdppr_prepared.join(codelist_smoking, on='code', how='inner')

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md ##4.2 Selection groups

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md Now we assign selection groups in order to identify an individual's censoring date in relation to the closest record date (to baseline) in the highest priority group.
# MAGIC   1. -20 <= x < 0 (20 years before baseline)
# MAGIC   2. 0 <= x < +0.25 (3 months after baseline)
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Note that smoking groups are not treated independently. We are finding an individual's censoring date across all smoking groups.

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Assign selection groups

# add a selection group to allow prioritisation of the different time periods around the study start date
# 1: -infinity <= x < 0 (all years before)
# 2: 0 <= x < +0.25 (3 months after)
# where x is the difference in years from the DATE to the study start date
smoking_selection_groups = (
    gdppr_smoking
    .withColumn('selection_group',
              f.when((f.col('DATE')  >= smoking_start_date) & (f.col('DATE') < f.col('entry_date')), 1)
              .when((f.col('DATE')  >= f.col('entry_date')) & (f.col('DATE') < smoking_end_date), 2)
              .otherwise(-1))
    .withColumn('diff_abs', f.abs(f.datediff(f.col('DATE'), f.col('entry_date'))/365.25))
)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Select the smoking record with highest priority
smoking_window = (
    Window
    .partitionBy('PERSON_ID')
    .orderBy(f.col("PERSON_ID"), f.col('selection_group'),f.col("diff_abs").asc())  
)

smoking_prioritised = (
    smoking_selection_groups
    .withColumn('_rank', f.dense_rank().over(smoking_window))
    .where(f.col('_rank') == 1)
    .drop('_rank')
)

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md ## 4.3 Smoking history censoring date
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Given the highest priority smoking record per patient, we store the date of that record. This will be the "censoring date" for the patient's smoking history. We use this patient-individual date to further prepare GDPRR (filtering out records dated after that censoring date).

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Obtain patient-specific smoking history censoring date
smoking_individual_censor_dates = (
    smoking_prioritised
    .select(f.col("PERSON_ID"),f.col("DATE").alias("CENSOR_DATE_END"))
)

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md ##4.4 Full smoking history
# MAGIC
# MAGIC We use the censoring dates to extract each patient's full smoking history from GDPPR. First we filter GDPPR to just all records up to the patient-individual censoring date for each patient. Then we finally match with the smoking codelist. 

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Prepare GDPPR
# Filter GDPPR to exclude records > than an individual's CENSOR_DATE_END - note gdppr here includes all codes (not just smoking)

gdppr_censored = (
    gdppr_prepared
    .join((smoking_individual_censor_dates), on=["PERSON_ID"], how="inner")
    .where(f.col('DATE') <= f.col('CENSOR_DATE_END'))
)

